lm). # Connection with Ancient Greek χάλιμα (khálima) can only be justified as a borrowing from it. # Akin to Sanskrit आल (āla, “poison”). # Akin to Ancient Greek σκάλμη (skálmē, “Thracian knife”). Possibly akin to halbë (“scab, scale on the skin”), halë (“bone”), hell (“skewer, pike”), dialectal helmë (“ax edge”). These would make the original sense “(poisoned) weapon”, only later becoming “poison”. Most likely continues substantivized adjective Proto-Albania…","tpl":[{"k":76,"lang":"sq"},{"k":29,"lang":69,"form":"scalmo","gloss":"plague"},{"k":29,"lang":"de","form":"Schelm"},{"k":29,"lang":45,"form":"χάλιμα"},{"k":29,"lang":"sa","form":"आल","gloss":"poison"},{"k":29,"lang":45,"form":"σκάλμη","gloss":"Thracian knife"},{"k":35,"lang":36,"form":"*helmV-","gloss":"cutting, biting"},{"k":35,"lang":38,"form":"*(s)kólh₃-mi-"}]},"rel":{"syn":["zeher","hidhërim","pikëllim","hall","nevojë"]}},{"w":"helm","p":"ADJ","s":[{"g":"very bitter"},{"g":"very sad, sorrowful, grievous"}],"f":[["helme",1]],"ety":{"text":"Uncertain, possibly a formation in -më. Several hypotheses have been proposed: # Akin to Old High German scalmo (“plague”) (German Schelm). # Connection with Ancient Greek χάλιμα (khálima) can only be justified as a borrowing from it. # Akin to Sanskrit आल (āla, “poison”). # Akin to Ancient Greek σκάλμη (skálmē, “Thracian knife”). Possibly akin to halbë (“scab, scale on the skin”), halë (“bone”), hell (“skewer, pike”), dialectal helmë (“ax edge”). These would make the original sense “(poisoned) weapon”, only later becoming “poison”. Most likely continues substantivized adjective Proto-Albania…","tpl":[{"k":76,"lang":"sq"},{"k":29,"lang":69,"form":"scalmo","gloss":"plague"},{"k":29,"lang":"de","form":"Schelm"},{"k":29,"lang":45,"form":"χάλιμα"},{"k":29,"lang":"sa","form":"आल","gloss":"poison"},{"k":29,"lang":45,"form":"σκάλμη","gloss":"Thracian knife"},{"k":35,"lang":36,"form":"*helmV-","gloss":"cutting, biting"},{"k":35,"lang":38,"form":"*(s)kólh₃-mi-"}]},"rel":{"d":["